{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774726,"nonce":"4s2aXJFAgGyQqCStUWBPcYd9360=","title":"fix: executor decorators must forward ADR-0058 service methods","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #52 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/adr-0058-service-executor-forwarding` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-21T16:16:00Z · Merged: 2026-07-21T17:37:43Z\n\nRunning a pipeline with a **shared service** (e.g. postgres) on the **k8s backend** failed with:\n\n\u003e failed to launch step: this executor does not support shared services (container images need the k8s backend)\n\n…even though the k8s executor fully supports shared services. Hit while dogfooding on colima.\n\n`scarab-server` wraps the real executor in two decorators — `SecretInjectingExecutor` and `CloneEnrichingExecutor`. ADR-0058 (PR #51) added `launch_service` / `service_ready` / `teardown_service` / `service_log_stream` to the `Executor` trait **with default impls**, and the default `launch_service` *rejects* shared services. Neither decorator overrode them, so the outermost decorator's reject-default **shadowed** the k8s executor's real implementation. `SCARAB_EXECUTOR=k8s` didn't matter — the wrapper swallowed it.\n\nThis is the same forward-or-drop hazard as the historical \"`SecretInjectingExecutor` dropped results\" bug. PR #51's service tests used a bare `FakeExecutor` and bypassed the decorators, so CI stayed green.\n\nBoth decorators now forward all four service methods to `self.inner`.\n\n`crates/scarab-server/tests/decorator_forwarding.rs` (+ an inline test for the non-exported `CloneEnrichingExecutor`) wraps a service-supporting `FakeExecutor` in each decorator and asserts `launch_service` reaches the inner executor instead of hitting the reject-default.\n\n`just check` green; `cargo test -p scarab-server` = 174 passed / 1 ignored.\n\nFollow-up to #51 (ADR-0058, git-bug 58646c1).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}